<title>NORWAY: FOKUS H1 PRE-TAX PROFITS RISE.</title>
<headline>FOKUS H1 PRE-TAX PROFITS RISE.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>				    (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Net interest</p>
<p> and credit commission	467	vs	463</p>
<p> Other operating income     284	vs	219</p>
<p> Operating expenses	   469	vs	406</p>
<p>Operating result</p>
<p> before losses/writedowns   282	vs	276</p>
<p> Pre-tax result		 301	vs	261</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's fourth largest bank is Fokus Bank ASA. It was expected to post a first-half 1997 pre-tax profit of 327 million crowns, according to a consensus poll of five analysts.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
